From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
Date: Fri, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] configfile: use read_file() on Python 3, readfp() on Python 2

`configparser.RawConfigParser.readfp()` was deprecated in Python 3.2
and **removed in Python 3.12**.  Klipper v0.11.0 calls it
unconditionally, so on Python 3.12+ (we ship Python 3.14) klippy aborts
at first config load with:

    AttributeError: 'ConfigParser' object has no attribute 'readfp'

Backport of upstream Klipper PR #6388
(https://github.com/Klipper3d/klipper/pull/6388) — the exact change
landed in upstream master at klippy/configfile.py:165-169.  Picks
read_file() on Python 3, falls back to readfp() on Python 2 so the
patch is harmless on the unlikely case anyone runs v0.11.0 on Python 2.

Signed-off-by: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
---
 klippy/configfile.py | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/klippy/configfile.py b/klippy/configfile.py
--- a/klippy/configfile.py
+++ b/klippy/configfile.py
@@ -213,7 +213,10 @@ class PrinterConfig:
         data = '\n'.join(buffer)
         del buffer[:]
         sbuffer = io.StringIO(data)
-        fileconfig.readfp(sbuffer, filename)
+        if sys.version_info.major >= 3:
+            fileconfig.read_file(sbuffer, filename)
+        else:
+            fileconfig.readfp(sbuffer, filename)
     def _resolve_include(self, source_filename, include_spec, fileconfig,
                          visited):
         dirname = os.path.dirname(source_filename)
-- 
